{
 "_note": "OFFSET MATH — the one function every other file in this corpus builds on. Raw offsets keep their SIGN (rubber-band over-scroll is real, and <CollapsingHeader stretch> is built on it); `progress` is computed from the CLAMPED offset so it never leaves 0..1. atTop/atBottom carry a HALF-POINT tolerance: momentum deceleration lands a fraction of a point short of the rail and a strict comparison makes `atBottom` flicker false at rest, which is how an infinite-scroll trigger misses. THE DEGENERATE CASE IS PINNED ON PURPOSE: content no taller than the viewport reports atTop AND atBottom (a page with nothing to scroll IS at both of its ends, and that is what makes on:reachEnd fire once for a short list) and progress 0, NOT 1 — a non-scrollable plane must publish the RESTING state, because a header that boots into its collapsed look on a short page is the visible bug. Non-finite input reads as the origin. Cases are a geometry -> the derived metrics. Runners: TS (packages/kernel/src/scroll.ts), Kotlin (:core ScrollLinkedConformanceTest), Swift (ScrollLinked.swift, record lane).",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "resting at the origin of a long page",
   "geometry": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "viewportWidth": 390,
    "viewportHeight": 800,
    "contentWidth": 390,
    "contentHeight": 2000
   },
   "expect": {
    "x": 0.0,
    "y": 0.0,
    "maxX": 0.0,
    "maxY": 1200.0,
    "progress": 0.0,
    "progressX": 0.0,
    "atTop": true,
    "atBottom": false,
    "atStart": true,
    "atEnd": true
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "mid-scroll",
   "geometry": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 600,
    "viewportWidth": 390,
    "viewportHeight": 800,
    "contentWidth": 390,
    "contentHeight": 2000
   },
   "expect": {
    "x": 0.0,
    "y": 600.0,
    "maxX": 0.0,
    "maxY": 1200.0,
    "progress": 0.5,
    "progressX": 0.0,
    "atTop": false,
    "atBottom": false,
    "atStart": true,
    "atEnd": true
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "exactly at the bottom",
